# Who gets asked to review what, in two-web.
#
# Handles here are individual GitHub accounts, not teams. The TogetherWeOwn org
# has no teams and one member with write access, so a team would be a group of
# one and would only add a layer to keep in sync. When a second person has write
# access, promote the functions that genuinely have two people to real teams —
# the path rules below are already split along those lines, so that change is one
# handle per line and nothing else.
#
# This file auto-requests the owner as a reviewer when a PR opens. Keep it
# accurate so the right reviewer is asked. Whether that review is additionally
# *required* to merge is set by the branch protection rule on `main` — see
# `docs/ci.md` for the required-checks list.
#
# A rule naming an account without write access to this repo is silently dropped
# by GitHub — no warning, no reviewer. That is exactly how this file broke: it
# named teams in the old two-gaming org, none of which exist here.

# Default: the application.
*                             @Rick7C2

# Anything a member sees: markup, styles and JS. Views call into the backend, so
# frontend and backend concerns meet here.
/resources/views/             @Rick7C2
/resources/js/                @Rick7C2
/resources/css/               @Rick7C2
/vite.config.js               @Rick7C2
# No tailwind.config.js on purpose: Tailwind 4 is configured from
# resources/css/app.css, which the rule above already covers.

# Backend: schema, policies, and the request path.
/app/                         @Rick7C2
/routes/                      @Rick7C2
/database/                    @Rick7C2
/config/                      @Rick7C2

# Tests and CI. "Make CI green" is the easiest thing in the repo to get wrong on
# purpose, so these paths are called out even though the owner is the same.
/tests/                       @Rick7C2
/.github/workflows/           @Rick7C2
/phpunit.xml                  @Rick7C2
/phpunit.dusk.xml             @Rick7C2
/phpstan.neon                 @Rick7C2
/pint.json                    @Rick7C2

# The boundary with the bot. The website reads the bot's contract and must never
# hold the bot token.
# app/Services/Discord/ does not exist yet — it arrives with TWO-24.
/config/services.php          @Rick7C2
/app/Services/Discord/        @Rick7C2

# Secrets posture.
/.env.example                 @Rick7C2
/.gitignore                   @Rick7C2
